IMPORTANT LIMITATION/BLOCKER FOR STRONGER POLICY:
Hash I/O uncertainty uses EXACT ORIGINAL maxmtime fallback, not a content tag.
It cannot alias a known content tag. Repeated unknown states may still compare
equal under original timestamps. Guaranteed fresh-on-every-unknown behavior is
NOT implemented. If root requires it, promotion is blocked pending a protocol
cold/reject signal or explicitly approved unique-generation mechanism. Do not
silently claim this fallback guarantees a new worker on every I/O error.
Content identity is not a full toolchain ABI safety proof.

Source and artifact edits STOP after this RELEASE. Root owns further validation.
